  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image shows Nancy Pelosi smiling while speaking at a podium, with overlaid text that reads 'don't worry we put an exclusion for white males in our anti-hatred resolution.' This meme is harmful because it falsely implies that the anti-hatred resolution excludes white males, which is a distortion of the actual content of such resolutions. The intent is to mock or undermine the seriousness of anti-hatred legislation by suggesting it is exclusionary or biased toward white males, thereby trivializing the issue of systemic racism and hate crimes. The meme uses the image of a political figure to convey a message that is misleading and potentially inflammatory, aiming to provoke controversy or skepticism about the fairness of anti-hate laws. The overall intent is to spread misinformation and cynicism about the purpose of anti-hate legislation, which can contribute to a hostile environment and discourage genuine efforts to combat hate.",
